    <!-- ─── Execution Sandbox Deep-Dive ────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="sandbox" class="py-24 px-6 border-t border-edge bg-surface/30">
        <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
            <div class="mb-12">
                <span class="font-mono text-2xs text-accent uppercase tracking-widest block mb-2 font-semibold">// sandboxed compute</span>
                <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-semibold text-snow">4-Tier Containment Architecture</h2>
                <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-2 max-w-2xl">
                    Every code execution job is isolated through defense-in-depth boundaries designed to prevent container breakouts, denial of service, and ambient privilege leakage.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
                
                <div class="bg-card border border-edge p-6 rounded space-y-3">
                    <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
                        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-snow font-medium">1. Bubblewrap 0.12.0 Namespaces</span>
                        <span class="text-2xs font-mono text-success bg-success/10 px-2 py-0.5 rounded border border-success/20">Enforced</span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
                        Spawns runtimes inside dedicated PID, IPC, UTS, and mount namespaces without setuid permissions. The host filesystem is mounted strictly read-only (`/usr`, `/lib`, `/bin`), `/tmp` is provisioned as an isolated `tmpfs`, and user workspaces are bound with noexec flags during execution.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="bg-card border border-edge p-6 rounded space-y-3">
                    <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
                        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-snow font-medium">2. Linux cgroup v2 Controllers</span>
                        <span class="text-2xs font-mono text-success bg-success/10 px-2 py-0.5 rounded border border-success/20">Delegated</span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
                        The container daemon creates an unprivileged `$ENGINE_CGROUP/server` scope owned by UID `10001 (engine)` before dropping privileges. Child runner processes are attached to sub-cgroups (`cg_e_xxx`) with aggregate limits on memory (`memory.max`), process count (`pids.max`), and CPU time, eliminating `EACCES (os error 13)` permission errors.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="bg-card border border-edge p-6 rounded space-y-3">
                    <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
                        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-snow font-medium">3. Seccomp-BPF & prlimit Guard</span>
                        <span class="text-2xs font-mono text-success bg-success/10 px-2 py-0.5 rounded border border-success/20">Filtered</span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
                        Enforces kernel-level BPF syscall filters that immediately kill processes attempting `ptrace`, `chroot`, `mount`, or raw socket creation. Secondary `prlimit` limits enforce maximum open file descriptors (512) and process counts (96-128) per runner invocation.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="bg-card border border-edge p-6 rounded space-y-3">
                    <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
                        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-snow font-medium">4. PUBLIC_URL Origin Lockdown</span>
                        <span class="text-2xs font-mono text-success bg-success/10 px-2 py-0.5 rounded border border-success/20">Locked</span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
                        The execution engine rejects all untrusted browser requests with `403 Forbidden` if their `Origin` or `Referer` headers do not match the authorized `PUBLIC_URL` policy. Backend server-to-server calls authenticate via `Authorization: Bearer <AUTH_TOKEN>`.
                    </p>
                </div>

